Each has a local proof producer and hosted delivery verification path.

## Request-ID Propagation

Threads a durable internal request-id through:

- Worker fetch
- Route helpers
- Problem details
- Server-action error logging
- Next request instrumentation

Use the existing request-id helpers — don't invent new correlation IDs.

## Performance Observability

```bash
bun run perf:measure-routes            # route transition timing
bun run perf:check-routes              # route transition readiness
bun run perf:dashboard-query-count     # workshop dashboard query audit
bun run perf:seed-fixture              # seed performance test data
bun run perf:library-baseline          # library performance baseline
bun run perf:profile-peak-load         # peak load profiling
bun run perf:collect-live-evidence     # live DB performance evidence
```

Performance evaluators for authenticated routes must name: auth/session setup, fixture identity, warmup behavior, sample count, and exact p50/p95 statistic definitions.
